BUILD_ONLY: the evaluator ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:control-transfer-<images/control-transfer/VERSION> is never published
(docs/protocol/README.md §1). An evaluation host builds it (images/control-transfer/README.md), or takes it from the
organization's own non-public copy of the package; the roboEngineer Control Transfer tasks reference that tag and Harbor
finds it in the local Docker image store. The agents' bases built from the same Dockerfile, efe:control-transfer-<VERSION>-nominal
and the G1 family's -train, hold public assets only and are public (build.sh).

Why
  The evaluator stage holds the Neural Fly force surrogate (forces.npz), fitted by calibrate_fly.py to the Neural-Fly
  flight logs (github aerorobotics/neural-fly, pinned commit), whose terms allow personal / educational use only
  ("written permission from the authors is required for further use"), so the fit is not redistributed. The nominal stage holds only public assets (Unitree mjlab G1 subset: Apache-2.0;
  MuJoCo Menagerie unitree_go2: BSD-3-Clause; skydio_x2: Apache-2.0): public.

What the builder needs
  git, python3 and network access to github.com and PyPI: fetch_assets.sh stages everything public from pinned upstream
  commits (checked), then build.sh. The force fit is not distributed: fetch_assets.sh --fit-fly downloads the public
  flight logs and fits it locally (calibrate_fly.py in a python:3.12.14-slim container, numpy 2.3.1 / mujoco 3.5.0;
  byte-identical to the pinned asset); docker is needed for that step. Its digest is pinned in each Neural Fly task's
  environment/sim/scripts/control_transfer/trusted/fly.py ASSET_SHA256 (the evaluator checks it at start), and
  fetch_assets.sh checks it too.
